     8	//! U2 adds the APIC water transfers: quadratic B-spline P2G with fixed-point atomics, grid
     9	//! gravity + boundary conditions, APIC G2P with a per-particle affine C matrix
    10	//! (`transfers.wgsl`). Per frame: `grid_clear → p2g_water → grid_update → g2p_water`, one
    11	//! substep (the CFL substep policy is a later-unit decision).
    12	//!
    13	//! U3 adds incompressibility (`pressure.wgsl`, KTD-2): a coarse-grid pressure seed plus a
    14	//! fixed budget of fine damped-Jacobi sweeps on ONE discretely consistent operator family
    15	//! (pressure at cell centers, corner-trilinear D, G = −Dᵀ by construction, A only ever the
    16	//! composition −D·M̃⁻¹·G) — no converged Poisson anywhere (R7). The full operator-family and
    17	//! coarse-seed construction is documented at the top of `pressure.wgsl`; the pre-registered
    18	//! gates live in `tests/twofield_pressure.rs`. The KTD-2 adaptive-Tait predictor is a STUB
    19	//! DECISION: deliberately not implemented (knob grid pins Tait ∈ {off}); if a later unit
    20	//! demonstrates an iteration-budget win it ships behind an opt-in `Config` gate, otherwise it
    21	//! is removed rather than shipped dormant.
    22	//!
    23	//! U4 (the L0 exit) adds pour emission and the pour-cavity machinery (`surface.wgsl`,
    24	//! KTD-6): `EmissionInput` drives the xpbd-shaped volume-consistent arclength-credit emitter
    25	//! into a pre-allocated water pool (water live range `[0, water_count)` grows toward
    26	//! `water_capacity`; solids sit AFTER the full pool so the KTD-1 range layout survives
    27	//! emission — dormant slots are never dispatched); enclosed air pockets are detected by a
    28	//! fixed-budget grid flood fill from the open (top) boundary and carried as ONE constraint
    29	//! bubble: a single Lagrange-multiplier scalar λ_b whose value IS the pocket pressure,
    30	//! represented identically in the coarse solve and the fine sweeps (see surface.wgsl's
    31	//! BUBBLE REPRESENTATION header). Gates: `tests/twofield_cavity.rs`.
    32	//!
    33	//! U6 (the early-L2 risk spike, run against a RIGID, kinematically frozen skeleton —
    34	//! KTD-3/KTD-4/KTD-8) adds `coupling.wgsl`: a thin solid-mass P2G (`p2g_solid` scatters the
    35	//! grain sphere volume π/6·d³ into a one-lane fixed-point field → local φ_s/φ_f per node)
    36	//! and the forced Laibe-Price exponential drag fold (`drag_fold`, which also owns the grid
    37	//! forces + BCs so the fold integrates the gravity source exactly). β(φ) mirrors
    38	//! `models::permeability` (Kozeny-Carman) blended toward a Wen-Yu dilute rate below
    39	//! φ_s ≈ 0.2 (Huilin-Gidaspow). The projection becomes the MIXTURE family ∇·(φ_f·v_f) = s
    40	//! (v_s = 0) with the velocity correction Δv = −(Δt_eff/ρ_w)∇p, Δt_eff = (1−e^{−βΔt})/β —
    41	//! the same integrator weight as the fold, carried as ς inside M̃⁻¹; φ NEVER scales the
    42	//! correction. Every impulse the frozen skeleton absorbs (drag pair + pressure on the solid
    43	//! volume) is recorded in the per-node `react` ledger — never discarded. Free water
    44	//! (φ_f = 1, ς = 1) is exact-zero passthrough, gated bitwise. Gates:
    45	//! `tests/twofield_coupling.rs`.
    46	//!
    47	//! U5 (rung L1, `plasticity.wgsl` + the CPU twin `plasticity.rs`) makes the solid phase a
    48	//! real elastoplastic granular material behind `Config::solid_dynamics` (default OFF — the
    49	//! U6 frozen-skeleton semantics are preserved bitwise; the dry-bed L1 scenes opt in): solid
    50	//! P2G with momentum + APIC + MLS-MPM fused stress force (`p2g_solid_dyn` replaces the
    51	//! frozen `p2g_solid` 1:1), grid forces + over-packing solids-pressure guard + Coulomb wall
    52	//! friction (`solid_update`), solid G2P with the deformation-gradient update, one 3×3 SVD
    53	//! per grain, and the Klar 2016 Drucker-Prager 3-branch return map + compaction-cap tamping
    54	//! memory (`g2p_solid`). The solid velocity does NOT yet enter the mixture divergence and
    55	//! the drag fold keeps its frozen-skeleton form — both are U7 scope (the L1 scenes are dry).
    56	//! Gates: `tests/twofield_bed.rs`.
