     1	# Reduce fixed-point atomic P2G contention
     2	
     3	## Tags
     4	
     5	- `physics:solver-performance`
     6	- `physics:numerics`
     7	- `physics:memory-layout`
     8	
     9	## Severity
    10	
    11	High
    12	
    13	## Problem
    14	
    15	The P2G pass scatters each water particle to a 3x3x3 stencil and atomically adds
    16	fixed-point mass, momentum, and volume lanes into the grid. This is portable in
    17	WebGPU but expensive in dense regions, and it depends on fixed-point headroom to
    18	avoid integer overflow.
    19	
    20	## Proposed fix
    21	
    22	Evaluate ways to reduce global atomic pressure without compromising MPM
    23	behavior:
    24	
    25	1. Particle binning by cell or tile so neighboring particles are processed more
    26	   coherently.
    27	2. Tile-local accumulation in workgroup memory followed by fewer global atomic
    28	   writes.
    29	3. Reduced or reorganized grid lanes if pressure/packing redesigns make some
    30	   lanes less hot.
    31	4. Explicit profiling before and after, with dense-bed and center-pour scenes.
    32	
    33	## Acceptance criteria
    34	
    35	- P2G produces equivalent mass/momentum transfer within test tolerances.
    36	- Dense regions show lower P2G GPU time or lower atomic-overflow risk.
    37	- Fixed-point bounds and overflow metrics remain documented.

