     1	# Split the monolithic MPM bind group by pass family
     2	
     3	## Tags
     4	
     5	- `physics:memory-layout`
     6	- `ui:device-compatibility`
     7	
     8	## Severity
     9	
    10	High
    11	
    12	## Problem
    13	
    14	The current MPM compute bind group exposes almost all simulation buffers to all
    15	compute pipelines. The project already requests a higher storage-buffer limit
    16	because the pipeline is near adapter limits. This makes future solver work
    17	fragile: adding one more storage buffer can break validation on constrained
    18	WebGPU adapters.
    19	
    20	## Proposed fix
    21	
    22	Split compute resources by pass family instead of binding everything
    23	everywhere:
    24	
    25	1. Particle transfer bind group: particles, affine, grid, grid velocities.
    26	2. Grid/pressure bind group: grid, grid velocities, classification/SDF, metrics.
    27	3. Bed/extraction bind group: particles or bed particles, bed lookup, bed delta,
    28	   bed extraction state.
    29	4. Render-packing bind group: particles, affine, bed extraction state,
    30	   `render_data`, metrics if still needed.
    31	
    32	This may require splitting the WGSL shader into pass-family modules or using
    33	multiple bind group layouts.
    34	
    35	## Acceptance criteria
    36	
    37	- No individual compute pipeline requires unnecessary storage buffers.
    38	- Required WebGPU limits are equal to or lower than the current limit request.
    39	- Pipeline validation tests cover the new layout.

