     1	# Reduce pressure solve cost without depending on sparse-grid work
     2	
     3	## Tags
     4	
     5	- `physics:solver-performance`
     6	- `physics:numerics`
     7	
     8	## Severity
     9	
    10	High
    11	
    12	## Problem
    13	
    14	The pressure projection uses many red/black Gauss-Seidel pressure pairs per
    15	substep. With 10 substeps, this multiplies quickly, and each pair runs red and
    16	black passes over the grid. Sparse active-cell work is already in progress, so
    17	this issue should focus on pressure-specific convergence and scheduling rather
    18	than filing another sparse-grid task.
    19	
    20	## Proposed fix
    21	
    22	Evaluate pressure-specific improvements that are compatible with either dense or
    23	future sparse execution:
    24	
    25	1. Use residual metrics to adapt pressure iteration count more aggressively.
    26	2. Investigate cheaper convergence accelerators, such as warm-starting pressure
    27	   from the previous substep or over-relaxation.
    28	3. Prototype a pressure solver variant with better convergence per pass, such as
    29	   a coarse correction or multigrid-inspired path, if it can fit WebGPU binding
    30	   and memory limits.
    31	4. Keep pressure correctness observable through residual metrics and existing
    32	   physics regression tests.
    33	
    34	## Acceptance criteria
    35	
    36	- Production frames perform fewer pressure passes when residuals are already
    37	  acceptable.
    38	- Pressure residual metrics remain stable or improve for canonical debug scenes.
    39	- The fix does not depend on adding a second issue for active-cell/sparse-grid
    40	  work.

