   235	## Risks & Dependencies
   236	
   237	- 3D low-frequency incompressibility: pure-local-Jacobi PB-MPM is documented to leave ~1–5% bulk compressibility at few iterations (PBF/PB-MPM inherit Jacobi's slow low-frequency convergence). Mitigation: KTD4 / U7 contingency (coarse V-cycle). This is the single largest realism risk.
   238	- Assembled-cost blind spot: a single-phase ≤33 ms result does not bound the full two-velocity system. Mitigation: R4 cost projection is a gating deliverable, not an afterthought.
   239	- Fixed-point overflow on fast pours: the position-correction lanes are a new overflow surface the existing FP math doesn't cover. Mitigation: R7 probe (U5).
   240	- Storage-buffer ceiling: the assembled solver may exceed the 9-buffer grant. Mitigation: KTD5 pass-family split + ledger (U6); browser `request_device` verification before relying on >9.
   241	- 3D P2G atomic contention at 200k. Mitigation: KTD6 cell-sort before scatter.
   242	- `λ`-as-pore-pressure (origin KD5) is unproven — but it is *deferred* coupling work, not in this prototype; flagged so the follow-up plan owns the audit.
